                },
                "message": "Handle destruction of opaque cyfuncs safely during cleanup\n\nWith module state, it's possible that the utility code types\ntraverse/clear/dealloc may be called during destructor shutdown\nwhen the module state is no longer findable. This is especially\nan issue for the single-phase init mode, but I think is a\ngeneral problem.\n\nThe usual approach we've used in similar situations for heap-types\nis to bail out and not complete the destruction. For cyfunctions\nI think we understand the type hierarchy well enough make it work\nbut this may not generally be possible for all types.",
